{"uid":"app.py","name":"app.py","qualname":"app.py","kind":"module","file":"app.py","line":1,"end_line":408,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"app.py — Corrected with proper particle-conserving ansatz =======================================================================","description":"Root cause identified: The uccsd() function in molecular_sim.py implements\nsingles excitations incorrectly. For excitation (o→v), it does:\n    CNOT ladder → RY(v) → CNOT ladder inverse\nThis ADDS an electron at v without REMOVING from o, producing |1110⟩\ninstead of |0110⟩. The states reachable by uccsd never include |0110⟩\nor |1001⟩, which are exactly the states the dipole operator connects\nto |1100⟩ (HF). Hence <μ>=0 always, giving α=0.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["app.py::VQEResult","app.py::givens_single_excitation","app.py::particle_conserving_ansatz","app.py::StarkEvaluator","app.py::DipoleOperatorBuilder","app.py::PolarizabilityCalculator"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
